= Dawes Plan negotiation 

The Attorney General, Patrick Hastings has come out and advised the justice ministry to persue the prosecution of communist party co founder J.R Campbell on incitement to sedition following an article he published in the workers weekly calling on British soldiers to turn their guns on the "exploiters and capitalists." Hastings believes these charges are appropriate. However, there is a stir among certain backbenchers. MacDonald fears a mutiny. He's thinking of getting Hastings to withdraw the prosecution. This could become a media spectacle. How should this be handled?

- @sign_treaty: Foreign Minister Breitscheid will sign the treaty, of course.
